00:25:26.820 --> 00:25:47.700
<v Ira Glass>The parents in this next story do a lot of things that  are really just amazing. They actually reach outside their own species into a different species, adopt a baby, raise it, love it, without really thinking through the consequences. Which turn out to be big. Here are the hosts of Radiolab, Jad Abumrad and Robert Krulwich, and the story this baby, Lucy.
<v Ira Glass>接下来这个故事里的父母做了一些真正令人惊叹的事情。他们实际上超出了自己的物种，跨越到另一个物种，领养了一个婴儿，抚养它，爱它，却没有真正思考过后果。结果证明后果很大。这是《放射实验室》的主持人贾德·阿布姆拉德和罗伯特·克鲁维奇，以及这个婴儿露西的故事。

00:25:47.700 --> 00:25:50.280
<v Jad Abumrad>So let's just start at the beginning. Who is Lucy?
<v Jad Abumrad>那么让我们从头开始吧。露西是谁？

00:25:50.280 --> 00:26:00.190
<v Robert Krulwich>Lucy is a chimpanzee that actually, this was found out later, born to a circus entertainer. Born in their camp.
<v Robert Krulwich>露西是一只黑猩猩，实际上，这是后来才发现的，她出生于一个马戏团艺人。出生在他们的营地里。

00:26:00.190 --> 00:26:01.120
<v Jad Abumrad>What country are we in?
<v Jad Abumrad>我们在哪个国家？

00:26:01.120 --> 00:26:08.430
<v Robert Krulwich>In the US. They traveled up and down the East Coast, the [UNINTELLIGIBLE] Chimp Arc Show, something like that. They were very popular.
<v Robert Krulwich>在美国。他们在东海岸巡回演出，什么什么黑猩猩秀，之类的。他们非常受欢迎。

00:26:08.430 --> 00:26:17.240
<v Robert Krulwich>We heard about Lucy from Charles Siebert, he's a reporter. And he tells the tale of a chimpanzee. She was a chimpanzee born-- do you know Jad?
<v Robert Krulwich>我们是从查尔斯·西伯特那里听说露西的，他是一名记者。他讲述了一个黑猩猩的故事。她是一只黑猩猩出生——你知道吗，贾德？

00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:19.860
<v Jad Abumrad>1964.
<v Jad Abumrad>1964年。

00:26:19.860 --> 00:26:24.730
<v Robert Krulwich>This is an early version of a chimp raised entirely in a human environment.
<v Robert Krulwich>这是早期完全在人类环境中抚养的黑猩猩之一。

00:26:24.730 --> 00:26:32.350
