<v Roger Fouts>Right.
<v Roger Fouts>对。

00:30:00.180 --> 00:30:11.680
<v Jad Abumrad>And at the time, he was the guy. He had just been part of a team that had proven for the first time the chimps could use sign language to communicate. So his job with Lucy was to teach her how to sign.
<v Jad Abumrad>当时，他就是专家。他刚参与了一个团队，首次证明了黑猩猩可以使用手语进行交流。所以他与露西的工作就是教她如何打手语。

00:30:11.680 --> 00:30:18.500
<v Roger Fouts>And I think I came into her life when she was-- as I remember, it was 1970. I think it was four or five. She was four or five years old.
<v Roger Fouts>我想我进入她生活的时候，她——我记得是1970年。我想她当时四五岁。她四五岁大。

00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:25.340
<v David Garland>Roger taught her signs for airplane, baby doll, ball, banana, barrette, berry, bird.
<v David Garland>罗杰教她“飞机”、“洋娃娃”、“球”、“香蕉”、“发夹”、“浆果”、“鸟”的手语。

00:30:25.340 --> 00:30:26.990
<v Roger Fouts>Yeah, so I was sort of like--
<v Roger Fouts>是的，所以我就像是——

00:30:26.990 --> 00:30:28.350
<v David Garland>Blanket.
<v David Garland>毯子。

00:30:28.350 --> 00:30:37.610
<v Roger Fouts>--the tutor friend, babysitter that would come over for a few hours each day and spend some time just playing with Lucy. I would work on signs.
<v Roger Fouts>——那个每天过来陪她玩几个小时的导师、朋友、保姆。我会教她手语。

00:30:37.610 --> 00:30:39.000
<v David Garland>Cat.
<v David Garland>猫。

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:44.690
<v Roger Fouts>We'd read books together, or we'd go for walks. I would chat with her basically.
<v Roger Fouts>我们会一起读书，或者去散步。我基本上会和她聊天。

00:30:44.690 --> 00:30:46.550
<v David Garland>Cry. Dirty.
<v David Garland>哭。脏。

00:30:46.550 --> 00:30:47.540
<v Jad Abumrad>And he says that Lucy--
<v Jad Abumrad>他说露西——

00:30:47.540 --> 00:30:47.980
<v David Garland>Enough.
<v David Garland>够了。

00:30:47.980 --> 00:30:49.010
<v Jad Abumrad>Just sort of--
<v Jad Abumrad>简直就是——

00:30:49.010 --> 00:30:49.820
<v Roger Fouts>Picked it up.
<v Roger Fouts>学会了。

00:30:49.820 --> 00:30:50.080
<v Jad Abumrad>Picked it all up.
<v Jad Abumrad>全部学会了。

00:30:50.080 --> 00:30:52.130
<v Roger Fouts>It was like a game.
<v Roger Fouts>这就像个游戏。

00:30:52.130 --> 00:31:15.340
<v Charles Siebert>She learned some 250 signs. And the big question is, OK, so is it me or mimicry, or are they able to spontaneously create words and put some together in a new original way? And there's been a lot of anecdotal evidence that in fact, Lucy did spontaneously create words.
<v Charles Siebert>她学会了大约250个手语词汇。最大的问题是，好的，那是模仿，还是她们能够自发地创造词汇并以一种全新的原始方式将它们组合在一起？有很多轶事证据表明，实际上，露西确实自发地创造了词汇。

00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:27.010
<v David Garland>In a later session, when shown a piece of watermelon, Lucy tasted it and she called it candy drink. When shown an onion before Roger good teach her the ASL sign for onion, Lucy volunteered--
<v David Garland>在后来的一个环节中，当展示一片西瓜时，露西尝了尝，把它称为“糖果饮料”。在罗杰教她美式手语中“洋葱”的打法之前，当被展示一个洋葱时，露西主动给出了——

00:31:27.010 --> 00:31:28.300
<v Roger Fouts>Cry hurt food.
<v Roger Fouts>“哭痛食物”。

00:31:28.300 --> 00:31:29.000
<v Jad Abumrad>Wow.
<v Jad Abumrad>哇。

